b.add(432,'stopping-work-sign','Separate work on the object from energy delivered','A 2 kg body moving at 3 m/s is brought to rest without rotation or a change in potential energy; what is the net work done on the body and the positive energy transferred out?', ['−9 J of net work on the body; 9 J transferred out','9 J of net work on the body; 9 J transferred out','−6 J of net work on the body; 6 J transferred out','−18 J of net work on the body; 18 J transferred out'],0,'Net work on the body is its final kinetic energy minus its initial kinetic energy; energy transferred out is the positive magnitude of that decrease.',['K_initial=0.5×2×3²=9 J, so W_net=0−9=−9 J.','This reverses the sign of work done on a body that loses kinetic energy.','This uses mv rather than one-half mv²; mv has momentum units.','This omits the one-half in kinetic energy.'],typ='numerical',difficulty='easy',assumptions=['Treat the body as a translating rigid mass in an inertial frame; all net work is accounted for.'],steps=['K_initial=(1/2)(2 kg)(3 m/s)²=9 J.','K_final=0 J, so W_net=K_final−K_initial=−9 J.','The positive energy transferred out is 9 J.'],formulas=[formula('W_net=K_final−K_initial; K=(1/2)mv²',{'W_net':'net work done on the body','K':'translational kinetic energy','m':'mass','v':'speed'},{'W_net,K':'J','m':'kg','v':'m/s'},['Constant mass in an inertial frame.'])])
